# Disability amount and the Canada workers benefit disability supplement. Read in October 2026 on the
# CRA's TD1 forms for 2024, 2025 and 2026 (federal line 6, provincial and territorial lines 4 or 5),
# PE428 and NS428 for 2024 and 2025 (line 58440), the CRA's indexation page, Revenu Quebec's line 376
# help and guide TP-1.G-V 2024, Revenu Quebec's "Principal changes" for employers for 2025 and 2026
# (TP-1015.3-V amounts), and the CRA's Schedule 6 (5000-S6, 5005-S6, 5009-S6, 5014-S6, Step 3) for
# 2024 and 2025. Schedule 6 for 2026 is not published: the federal 2026 amounts are the indexation
# page's, with the 2025 rates; Quebec, Alberta and Nunavut keep their 2025 values.
#   fed.disability, prov.disability: the disability amount for a person 18 or older with an approved
#     Form T2201 (Quebec: the amount for a severe and prolonged impairment, line 376)
#   cwb.disability: the person's own working income above which it phases in; phase-in rate without an
#     eligible spouse; with one; maximum; adjusted family net income where the reduction starts for a
#     person alone; with a spouse; with an eligible dependant and no spouse; with both; reduction rate;
#     reduction rate when both spouses are eligible for the disability tax credit
rule tax.fed.disability AMOUNT
rule tax.prov.disability AMOUNT province
rule tax.cwb.disability LIST province

