# Minimum tax on donated securities, security options and the capital gains deduction (2024 rules).
# Read in October 2026 on the CRA's Form T691 for 2024 and 2025 and Revenu Quebec's TP-776.42-V 2025;
# Finances Quebec's Information Bulletin 2024-6 confirms Quebec follows the federal base from 2024
# (only its rate and exemption differ). The 2026 forms are not published: the 2025 values stay.
#   amt.gains, qc.amtGains: share of the capital gains on gifts of publicly listed securities added to
#     adjusted taxable income; share of the capital gains deduction (lifetime exemption) and of the security
#     options deduction for donated securities taken off it
rule tax.amt.gains LIST
rule tax.qc.amtGains LIST

tax.amt.gains | - | 2024-01-01 | 0.30; 0.40 | CRA, Form T691 2024 and 2025 (2025: lines 24 to 26, 30 %; line 31, 40 % of the security options deduction for donated securities; line 87, 40 % of line 25400); Income Tax Act s. 127.52(1)
tax.qc.amtGains | - | 2024-01-01 | 0.30; 0.40 | Revenu Québec, TP-776.42-V 2025, work charts 4 and 5 (lines 146.1 to 146.3, 30 %; lines 171.1 to 171.5, 40 %); Finances Québec, Information Bulletin 2024-6 (harmonized from 2024)
